<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="section-1" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Factoring</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      In this section we will focus on factoring, mainly the factoring 
      of quadratic expressions. By the end of this section we will have 
      developed a general factoring strategy that can be applied to all
      quadratic expressions and can extend to higher power expressions
      as well. Factoring is one of the ways to solve a quadratic equation,
      which will be the focus of our next section.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include href="./ws-1-1.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./ws-1-2.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./ws-1-3.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./ws-1-4.ptx" />
<subsection xml:id="subsec-factoring-strategy">
  <title>A Factoring Strategy</title>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <p>
        Check for a GCF and if there is one, factor it out.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        If there are two terms, check for a difference of squares and factor accordingly.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        If there are four (or six or eight...) terms, then factor by grouping.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        If there are three terms, check for a perfect square trinomial. See if the first and last terms are prefect squares and check to see if the middle term is <m>2acx</m>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        If a trinomial is not a perfect square trinomial and the first term has a coefficient of 1, then find two numbers that add to <m>b</m> and multiply to <m>c</m>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        If the trinomial is not a perfect square trinomial and the first term does not have a coefficient of 1, multiply the first and last number to get the key number. 
        Look for two numbers that multiply to the key number and add to the middle number. Split the middle term into two terms using these numbers. Then factor by grouping.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-Video-Examples-1">
    <title>Video Examples</title>
